<title>HUNGARY: Turkey bond issue a success - S&amp;P director.</title>
<headline>Turkey bond issue a success - S&amp;P director.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's $300 million bond issue earlier this week was well received on the Eurobond market, Standard &amp; Poor's director Stuart Shipperlee told a conference of Hungarian businessmen on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;This was perhaps the most successful bond in the last four weeks,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The five-year bonds were priced to yield 350 b.p. over the 6.625 percent April 2002 U.S. Treasury.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
